**What was proven:**

* The benchmark is not solved by candidate-only information.
* It is not solved by schema-only information.
* It is not solved by evidence-only without candidates.
* It is not solved by text-only baselines.
* It is not solved by single-view baselines.
* It is not solved by raw latent baselines.
* It is not solved by frozen hidden states alone.
* Trainable shared clones solve it much better.

**Important controls passed:**

```text
candidate_only: near chance
candidate_metadata_only: near chance
view_masked_candidates_visible: near chance
schema_only: near chance
