### 7. Physical role-order invariance was fixed and validated

**Proven in:** Stage 4.1 audit and corrected final Stage 4 report
**Main files/artifacts:**

```text
reports/STAGE41_PHYSICAL_ORDER_INVARIANCE_AUDIT.md
results/stage41_physical_order_invariance_audit.json
reports/STAGE4_FINAL_CANDIDATE_TOKEN_DIRECT_VALIDATION.md
```

**Bug found:**

```text
legacy evaluator permuted role_ids and clone_activations
but did not permute token_states or token_mask
```

**Corrected result:**

```text
normal mean:              0.7904
correct all-24 mean:      0.7904
canonicalized mean:       0.7904
legacy buggy mean:        0.2701
```

**What was proven:**

* The previous physical-order failure was an evaluator bug.
* After permuting all role-axis tensors together, all 24 role permutations match normal accuracy.
* The candidate-token-direct architecture is invariant to physical role ordering when evaluated correctly.

**Key implication:**

> The model is not relying on arbitrary role seat position. It uses role-aligned evidence correctly.

