## Main proven claims

### Strongly supported claim

> A shared-weight cloned transformer-like model can be trained so candidate-specific queries into its clones’ internal token states become useful for coordination, substantially outperforming an exact frozen same-architecture comparator and text/raw/single-view baselines on a clean schema-aware real-code import-restoration benchmark.

### Strongly supported numbers

```text
Stage 4 final:
trainable latent: 0.7892
frozen same architecture: 0.1518
text-only: 0.1256
chance: 0.1250
delta: +0.6374
CI: [0.4818, 0.7836]
wins: 10/10 seeds
```

### Stage 5 portfolio extension

```text
Stage 5 full 4-avenue:
trainable: 0.9144
frozen: 0.2655
delta: +0.6488

Stage 4 baseline:
trainable: 0.7892
frozen: 0.1518
delta: +0.6374
```

### Best concise summary

> Stage 4 proves trained latent coordination between shared-weight cloned agents on a clean real-code candidate-selection task. Stage 5 shows that letting each role explore multiple latent avenues improves the system as a portfolio/search mechanism.

