## What has **not** been proven yet

Do **not** claim these yet:

* Open-ended code repair.
* SWE-bench success.
* General coding-agent superiority.
* Human-level coding.
* Lower dollar cost in production.
* Faster wall-clock inference.
* Faster training.
* Scaling to thousands of full agents.
* Mandatory joint multi-avenue fusion.
* Full mechanistic interpretability.

---

## Current research position

The strongest current position is:

> Prior work has studied learned communication and latent inter-agent communication, but this project demonstrates a specific architecture-level proof: shared-weight cloned agents trained end-to-end for candidate-specific latent coordination, validated against frozen same-architecture, text, raw-latent, single-view, shortcut, corruption, invariance, leakage, and parameter-update controls on a clean real-code schema-aware benchmark.

That is the clean result.
